# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is committed so the
# config surface is discoverable on a fresh clone.
#
# Read by skillgrade (which threads these into the agent + grader environments)
# and auto-loaded by figma-browser/lib/connect.mjs for bare-shell CLI use.
#
# Precedence differs between those two, which matters the moment you try to
# override something on the command line:
#
#   bare CLI      a real environment variable WINS over .env  (connect.mjs)
#   skillgrade    .env WINS over the environment — providers/local.js spawns
#                 with { ...process.env, ...dotenv }, so
#                 `FIGMA_FILE_KEY=x npx skillgrade …` is silently ignored.
#                 Change the value in .env instead.

# --- Figma files (required) -----------------------------------------------
#
# One binding per design system, and that is the whole config surface:
#
#   FIGMA_FILE_<SLUG>   slug → file key. The map. Machine-specific, because a
#                       key identifies YOUR editable copy.
#
# Nothing passes a key between processes. Each dataset row carries a
# `figma_file` slug, the harness exports FIGMA_FILE=<slug> for the trial, and
# connect.mjs does the lookup. The slug is intrinsic to the question and lives
# in git; the key never leaves this file. Nobody can share a key; everybody
# shares the slug.
#
# connect.mjs config() resolves, in order:
#   1. --file=<slug>            explicit, for a human switching mid-session
#   2. FIGMA_FILE=<slug>        the harness per trial, or your own export
#   3. the sole FIGMA_FILE_*    if exactly one is bound — so a single design
#                               system needs no selector at all
#   4. error listing the bound slugs and asking for FIGMA_FILE=<slug>
#
# Slugs are uppercased to form the variable name:  figma_file: sds → FIGMA_FILE_SDS
# Human-facing names ("Simple Design System") live with the dataset, not here.
#
# Fill in only the slugs you actually have. An unbound slug is a hard error
# naming the variable to set, rather than a run that quietly reads the wrong
# document — filter it out instead: `node build-eval.mjs --figma_file=sds`.
#
# Every key MUST be an editable copy in the logged-in account. A community-file
# preview is view-only, has no window.figma, and the skill aborts rather than
# degrade to hex-scraping. The key is the segment after /design/ in the URL:
#
#   https://www.figma.com/design/<FILE_KEY>/Some-File-Name
#
# NOTE: answers are bound to a COPY, not to a design system. `open` rows grade
# on node ids, and duplicating the same file into another account produces
# different ids — so a fresh clone must re-run `node gen.mjs --write` against
# its own copies before the dataset grades correctly. Value rows (#2c2c2c,
# Space/200) survive duplication; id-based ones do not.

# figma_file: sds — Simple Design System
FIGMA_FILE_SDS=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# One line per additional design system you want to evaluate.
# FIGMA_FILE_MUI=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# FIGMA_FILE_KEY is GONE — delete it if your .env still has one. It used to be
# both the config and the wire, which is why a second design system did not fit:
# one variable cannot mean both "your copy" and "which design system this
# question is about". Setting it with no bindings present errors and names the
# rename, rather than quietly keeping a second source of truth alive.

# --- browser --------------------------------------------------------------

# Chrome executable for the dedicated browser. Absolute system path.
FIGMA_CHROME_BIN=/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome

# CDP port. Anything already listening here is reused as-is.
FIGMA_CDP_PORT=9333

# Where the logged-in Figma session is stored. Leave UNSET to use the default,
# which is repo-local (figma-skills/.chrome-profile) and gitignored — created by
# `node figma-browser/lib/figma.mjs login`. Set it only to reuse another profile.
# FIGMA_CHROME_PROFILE=/Users/you/.figma-chrome

# Multiple design systems share ONE Chrome: cdp.mjs picks the tab by URL
# substring, so keep a tab open per file and each trial attaches to its own.
# A file with no open tab still works — connect() opens one and waits — but the
# first trial on it pays that cold start.

# --- LangSmith (dataset host) ---------------------------------------------
#
# The dataset lives on LangSmith, not on disk — datasets/rows.jsonl is the
# local ancestor, the same way agent-plaform/evals/dataset.jsonl is.
#
# Use a PERSONAL-organization key, not a company one. LangSmith creates a
# personal org on first login, so an existing work login usually already has
# one: switch org at https://smith.langchain.com, then mint a key at
# https://smith.langchain.com/settings → API Keys.
#
# Pick a Personal Access Token (lsv2_pt_…) — the docs recommend PATs for
# personal scripts and tools. A service key (lsv2_sk_…) is for production
# services and needs an X-Tenant-Id header to say which workspace it means.
#
# Personal org: 1 workspace, no collaborators, Developer plan, and 5,000 unique
# traces/month on the free tier — about three full 328×5 runs.
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=lsv2_pt_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT=https://api.smith.langchain.com

# --- optional -------------------------------------------------------------

# Only the llm_rubric graders need this; deterministic graders and the agent
# (local Claude Code CLI) do not.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
